for the second time a jury has found  Monsanto's Roundup weedkiller played a  role in causing cancer  yesterday's unanimous decision  determined roundup caused or was a  substantial factor in causing  seventy-year-old  Edwin hardiman's non-hodgkins lymphoma  Anna Warner is here with how this  verdict could affect thousands of other  lawsuits claiming the herbicide causes  cancer yeah good morning good morning  this is just the first phase in  hardiman's case against Monsanto and its  new parent company Bayer which contains  roundups active ingredient glyphosate is  safe attorneys will now go back to the  jury to decide whether or not the  company is liable and has to pay  monetary damages Edwin hardiman's  attorneys say he started using roundup  products back in the 1980s to treat  poison oak and weeds on his property in  Northern California he continued to do  so until 2012 three years later he was  diagnosed with cancer roundup extended  control roundups manufacturer says its  product is not to blame  in a statement Monsanto's parent company  Bayer says we have great sympathy for  mr. Hardiman and his family but an  extensive body of science supports the  conclusion that roundup was not the  cause of his cancer the jury disagreed  unanimously deciding that roundup was  responsible this is the second time a  jury has ruled against the products  manufacturer in August of last year  duane lee johnson was awarded 289  million dollars in damages after the  Court determined roundup was also a  substantial factor in causing his  non-hodgkins lymphoma a judge later  lowered that award to 78 million dollars  and Monsanto has appealed  I spoke with Johnson last year what did  that verdict mean to you the verdict  really meant to me that this thing was  not done in vain and I remember standing  there saying to myself if I lose this  case this company is going to be able to  get away and then they'll be able to say  see I told you our stuff didn't do that  attorneys for Edwin Hartman say their  client is pleased with the verdict in a  phone interview co-counsel jennifer  moore says in the trials second phase  they'll seek to prove Monson  knowingly mislead the public they knew  for decades that roundup can cause  cancer and frankly they just didn't care  this is a big loss for Bayer and  Monsanto it proves that juries are being  convinced that roundup is causing cancer  and there's a lot at stake here Bayer is  facing more than 11,000 lawsuits  connected to roundup now it contends the  jury's decision Tuesday has no impact on  future cases and trials they say each  one is different legally and factually  and says more than 800 studies from  around the world confirm the product is  safe when used as directed but there's  not total agreement on that state of  California disagrees another world  agency at arm of the w-h-o disagrees it  seems like the jury didn't come to this  decision lightly either Anna thank you
 

